-- the form the two debts of the mixture layer force, and the last form of this spine. A rate has to read
-- what is dissolved and how much of it: a constituent should catalyse the change it actually catalyses
-- rather than every change at once, and a rate depends on how much base there is and not only on whether
-- there is any. So the medium belongs inside the argument a rate takes.
--
-- It cannot be the mixture of full records: a mixture holds substances, a substance holds motions, and a
-- motion's rate would take a situation holding the mixture, which is a cycle. What a rate needs of the
-- medium is not the records but the references -- which substances are present, how much, and whether a
-- chiral one is in excess. The records live in the graph and the medium names them, which is what a
-- reference is for.
--
-- a dissolved constituent as the observation records it: the tag naming the substance, the order of
-- magnitude of its concentration, and whether it is present in excess over its mirror image
Dissolved : Type 0
Dissolved = (tag : Nat) × ((amount : Nat) × Bool)
